nodecode-tabular is a rewrite of frankiethull's frankiethull/hermes-tabular:

  https://github.com/frankiethull/hermes-tabular
  commit c5b965086d0d5b8239703c2aa8a5df99b1eee5c3
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 hermes-tabular contributors (LICENSE)

skill/ is that repository's skills/, references/ and examples/ folders,
unchanged: the eleven SKILL.md files, defaults.yaml, pitfalls.md and the three
worked examples.

What was rewritten: the two steps of the pack that need no model. Its
"inspect" and "split" skills described profiling a table and holding out an
honest test set in Python; here they are one pass over one file in Lisp --
shape, per-column type, role, missingness and cardinality, duplicate rows,
leakage hints by name, the task the target implies, and the split and model
order the pack's own policy asks for -- plus a seeded, stratified split that
writes train and test files. The policy numbers in defaults.yaml are the same
numbers, kept in one Lisp parameter so the verb and the prose cannot drift.

What was left out: the models. CatBoost, TabICL, the linear baseline, the
ensemble and the joblib checkpoint are Python, and a rewrite that bundled a
Python runtime would be worse than the pack. The cell profiles, decides and
splits; fitting stays with whatever toolchain the project already has, and the
pack's prose in skill/ still tells the model how to do it. Also left out: the
Hermes-side install scripts (scripts/install_skills.py, validate_skills.py),
which only copied these Markdown files into a Hermes home.
